From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a dock is told only what changed in each frame

DisplayLinkManager used lots of CPU on lyra's dock. evdi passes each page
flip's FB_DAMAGE_CLIPS to it, and it compresses only that rect. Upstream
reads FB_DAMAGE_CLIPS only behind ChromeOS's PSR2 flag, so evdi got no clip
and marked the whole screen changed on every flip. With the flag, upstream
sent one clip for every flip: the first frame's rect, made once on the
first DRM device (crbug.com/572557701).

- `HardwareDisplayPlane::InitializeProperties` reads FB_DAMAGE_CLIPS on
  every plane that has it.
- `HardwareDisplayPlaneAtomic::AssignPlaneProps` makes a blob from each
  frame's damage on the plane's own device. The plane keeps it until its
  next assignment; a commit holds its own reference.
- No clip for empty damage or a turned plane: the kernel then takes the
  whole plane as changed.
- `FakeDrmDevice` names `FB_DAMAGE_CLIPS`.

Tested by `DrmDamageClipsTest`.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine job
builds it on `crux`.

Co-Authored-By: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011frZatTUhkRWKPdRizJWsH
